course: dictionary
lesson: 10072
title: Thankfulness: the feeling of being grateful
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Thankfulness is the feeling of being grateful and glad for something good. You can feel it for something you have, like a warm home, or for something someone has done for you, like a friend helping you up after a fall.
explain: Thankfulness is a noun that you cannot count, so you say «a feeling of thankfulness» or «with thankfulness», not «two thankfulnesses». Thankful is the adjective, and thank is the verb. Thankfulness is made from thankful with -ness added.
explain: Look at the words around it: «Thankfulness leads to kindness: we do not hurt living things for fun, and at harvest festival churches fill up with tins and bread to share.» The clues are kindness and sharing. Thankfulness makes people want to give to others.
fact: Thankfulness means being grateful and glad for something good.
fact: Thankfulness is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say «a feeling of thankfulness».
fact: Thankful is the adjective and thank is the verb; thankfulness comes from thankful.
fact: In church, thankfulness to God is shown in prayers, grace before meals and harvest festival.
fact: «Feeling small under the night sky can lead to wonder and thankfulness rather than fear.»
exercise: What does thankfulness mean? | Being worried about a test | Being tired after a long day | Being angry about something unfair | *Being grateful and glad for something good
exercise: In «Feeling small under the night sky can lead to wonder and thankfulness rather than fear», which feeling is thankfulness chosen instead of? | night | *fear | wonder | sky
exercise: Which is the correct way to use thankfulness? | thankfulnesses for my dog | a thankfulness for the sun | two thankfulnesses | *with thankfulness
test: At harvest festival, churches fill up with tins and bread to share with people who do not have enough. What does this show about thankfulness? | Thankfulness means being afraid of the dark | *Thankfulness can lead to sharing with people in need | Thankfulness only means saying sorry | Thankfulness is a kind of game
test: Which word is the noun for the feeling of being thankful? | *thankfulness | thank | thankful | thanked
exam: Which sentence uses thankfulness correctly? | She felt a thankfulness for her friend. | She has two thankfulnesses for her cat. | Thankfulness is running very fast. | *She felt great thankfulness for her friend's help.
